Commit:     welpy-cw <h.w.forms@arcor.de>
CommitDate: Sun Apr 19 20:04:00 2026 +0000

    Bug 1899236 - Refactor Gloda folder compaction pass into a lightweight GC and healing sweep. r=mkmelin


    Historically, the Gloda compaction pass assumed message keys in local folders
    acted as mbox offsets that shifted during compaction. This assumption is
    obsolete; `nsMsgDatabase` keys are stable.

    This patch removes the complex two-stream parallel merge between the folder
    enumerator and the Gloda database. The compaction pass now acts strictly as a
    Garbage Collection and Healing sweep:
    1. Garbage Collection: Verifies continued existence of known Gloda records via
       the rather inexpensive `nsMsgDatabase.containsKey()`.
    2. Healing: Utilizes a new "Limbo Cache" in PendingCommitTracker to safely
       restore wiped `gloda-id` commits when a compaction database-swap occurs.

    Performance & Stability Wins:
    - Fixes CPU/IO Thrashing (Bug 1995890): Eliminates the need to instantiate
      heavy `nsIMsgDBHdr` XPCOM objects for every message in the folder. Replaces
      string-based Message-ID lookups with instantaneous integer hash lookups.
    - Resolves XPCOM Exceptions & Console Spam (Bug 1963490): The Limbo Cache
      prevents `NS_ERROR_ILLEGAL_VALUE` exceptions by avoiding stale C++ pointers.
      Removing the fragile parallel-merge logic entirely eliminates "sketchy key"
      false alarms and synchronous MIME-decoding log spam.
    - Resolves Exceptions & Error Spam on Folder Deletion (Bug 1903744): Clears the
      PendingCommitTracker and Limbo Cache during `folderDeleted` notifications.
      This prevents dead database pointers from throwing exceptions during the async
      commit callback (silencing multiple error logs in different automated tests)
      and prevents memory leaks.
    - Clarifies Split-Brain Error Logging: Downgrades an outdated `.error()` in
      `_commitCallback` to a `.warn()` and updates comments to correctly document
      how Gloda safely self-heals orphaned .msf headers via SQLite deduplication.
    - Silences "Impossible Folder ID" Warnings: Purges orphaned background jobs when
      a folder is deleted, preventing the Gloda worker from attempting to process
      dead folders and safely keeping the console clean.
    - Eliminates Phantom DB Writes: Replaces the persistent `_kFolderCompactedFlag`
      bitmask with a transient in-memory boolean, saving a redundant SQLite write
      on every folder auto-compaction.
    - Expanded Coverage: Adds a dedicated unit test (`test_limbo_cache_healing`)
      to explicitly verify the compaction amnesia trap and healing mechanism.

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D294726

